meta {
  name: 01 List Samples (Listing & Filters)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples?page=1&limit=20
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 20
  ~search: ACC-00001
  ~status: NEW
  ~priority: ROUTINE
  ~collectionStatus: PENDING
  ~tatStatus: WITHIN
  ~orderId: {{orderId}}
  ~originBranchId: {{branchId}}
  ~processingBranchId: {{branchId}}
  ~patientId: {{patientPersonId}}
  ~referredByDoctorId: {{referralDoctorId}}
  ~referralPanelId: {{referralPanelId}}
  ~dateFrom: 2026-07-01
  ~dateTo: 2026-07-31
  ~departmentId: {{departmentId}}
  ~branchLabTestId: {{branchLabTestId}}
  ~branchLabPanelId: {{branchLabPanelId}}
  ~orderMode: Home Visit
  ~logisticsType: Courier
  ~reportStatus: SAVED
  ~isOutsource: false
  ~isUrgent: false
  ~isHomeCollection: false
  ~orderStatus: PARTIALLY_COMPLETED
  ~orderType: WALK_IN
  ~createdByUserId: {{userPersonId}}
  ~logisticsPerson: ravi
  ~storeLocation: freezer
  ~discardMethod: Autoclave
  ~containerTypes: URINE_CONTAINER
  ~sampleNames: Serum-Plain
  ~sampleNameNotSet: false
  ~sampleTypes: Serum
  ~sampleTypeNotSet: false
  ~categoryId: {{categoryId}}
  ~subCategoryId: {{subCategoryId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data[0]) {
    bru.setEnvVar("sampleId", data[0].id);
    bru.setEnvVar("accessionNo", data[0].accessionNo);
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("pagination meta is present", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().meta).to.have.property("total");
  });
  test("rows carry a derived tatStatus", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    if (d.length) expect(d[0]).to.have.property("tatStatus");
  });
}

docs {
  Paginated list of accession samples in the active branch (§A.6). Newest first.
  Each row is enriched with a derived `tatStatus` (§A.4 — `WITHIN` | `WARNING` |
  `CRITICAL` | `BREACHED` | `null` for terminal samples) and carries the linked
  `order` (with patient / referral) plus its `tests`. Captures `sampleId` +
  `accessionNo` from the first row for the action requests below.

  ## Filters (toggle the `~` to enable a query param)

  - `search` — matches barcode **or** order id (e.g. `ORD-00717`), plus patient name / UHID / mobile (case-insensitive). The accession number is NOT searched any more.
  - `status` — the §A.5 status tab (a `SampleStatus` — the 15-stage lifecycle).
  - `priority` — `ROUTINE` | `URGENT` | `STAT`.
  - `collectionStatus` — order-level **collection progress** `PENDING` | `PARTIAL`
    | `COLLECTED` (derived from the order's workflow items' `collectedAt`; distinct
    from `status`). Same rule as the Order Console's `sampleStatus`.
  - `tatStatus` — derived TAT band (translated to a `createdAt` range server-side).
  - `orderId` / `originBranchId` / `processingBranchId` — scoping filters.
  - `patientId` / `referredByDoctorId` / `referralPanelId` — via the linked order.
  - `dateFrom` / `dateTo` — linked order's `orderDate` range.
  - `departmentId` / `branchLabTestId` / `branchLabPanelId` — via the order's items.
  - `orderMode` — DEPRECATED (`Walk-in` | `Home Visit` | `Referral` | `Outsource` | `Emergency`); use `orderType` below. Kept only until the frontend stops sending it.
  - `logisticsType` — sample scalar filter (also matches the transfer's logistics type, see below).
  - `reportStatus` — one of the nine report statuses the Technician Reporting screen uses: `PENDING` | `PARTIAL_PENDING` | `SAVED` | `VALIDATION_PENDING` | `RESULT_DONE` | `APPROVED` | `PUBLISHED` | `ERROR_REPORTED` | `RESULT_REJECTED`. It reads the sample's real report (the sample's own `reportStatus` column is never written); a sample with no report yet matches no status. A panel member's sample matches its own member report.
  - `isOutsource` / `isUrgent` / `isHomeCollection` — boolean toggles.

  **New filters (2026-10).**
  - `orderStatus` — the ORDER's overall report progress (the Order Console's "Order Status"): `PENDING` | `PARTIALLY_COMPLETED` | `COMPLETED` | `APPROVED` | `PUBLISHED`. Derived from every test of the order by the same rule the Order Console uses; shows every row of a matching order. Different from `reportStatus`, which is one test's own report.
  - `orderType` — how the order came in: `WALK_IN` | `APP` | `WEBSITE` (the Registration "Order Type").
  - `createdByUserId` (UUID) — "Billed by": the person who created the order (`Order.createdBy`).
  - `logisticsPerson` — part of the logistics person's name, case-insensitive (matches the transfer of a sample that is Sent / Forwarded / Outsourced, or the sample's own column).
  - `storeLocation` — part of the storage location typed at Store, case-insensitive.
  - `discardMethod` — samples discarded with that method (matches the reason of the sample's `discard` history entry).
  - `containerTypes` — one or more `ContainerType` values (repeat the param).
  - `sampleNames` / `sampleTypes` — one or more values matched EXACTLY as stored (repeat the param; commas are kept). The options list merges spelling variants into one entry and sends all of that entry's variants. `sampleNameNotSet=true` / `sampleTypeNotSet=true` also include samples with no name / type (null or blank).
  - `categoryId` / `subCategoryId` (UUID) — samples of the tests in that category / subcategory; a test counts when the tenant test OR a branch copy of it is classified there.

  Requires a confirmed diagnostic order to exist first (Orders folder) so samples
  have been generated.

  **Same transfer + matched transfer (2026-10).** The transfer filters of one kind are met by ONE transfer: Sent To `destinationBranchId` + `sendDate` (INTERNAL), Forwarded To `externalPartnerName` + `forwardDate` (EXTERNAL), `outsourceCenterId` + `outsourceDate` (OUTSOURCE). So a sample sent to B on the 28th (B rejected it) and later to C on the 30th is found by "B + 28th" but NOT by "B + 30th". While any of these filters is on, every row also carries `matchedTransfer` (same fields as `transfers[0]`, with `destinationBranchName` / `outsourceCenterName`): the latest transfer that met the filter - of the kind that fits the row's status, else the newest. It can differ from `transfers[0]` (the live one): the row's label / Send details describe `matchedTransfer`, the row's actions keep following `transfers[0]`. Without a transfer filter the field is absent. `logisticsType` / `logisticsPerson` are still matched on any transfer of a sample that is out now (not tied to the matched one).

  **Where did I send it (sender's filters).** `destinationBranchId` (UUID): only samples Sent RIGHT NOW to that
  branch (status Sent + a live INTERNAL transfer to it; a sample the receiving branch sent back, "Sent - Repeated",
  still counts because it stays Sent until the sender decides; one the sender repeated or retrieved does not).
  `externalPartnerName`: only samples Forwarded right now to a partner whose name contains the text (case-insensitive,
  trimmed, max 200). `logisticsType`: now matches the TRANSFER's logistics type of a sample that is Sent / Forwarded /
  Outsourced (a Send, Forward or Outsource records the logistics on the transfer, never on the sample; the sample's
  own column is kept as an alternative for older rows). `outsourceCenterId` and `sendDate` / `forwardDate` /
  `outsourceDate` already filtered on the transfer. All of them also apply to `/summary` (the tab counts) and
  `/grouped`.

  **Stored / Discarded tab columns.** Every row carries `storeLocation` (the Storage Location typed at Store; kept after
  Discard). A row whose status is `DISCARDED` also carries `discardMethod` - the method picked at Discard, read from the
  sample's latest `discard` history entry (null if none; absent on every other status). Both the flat list and
  `/grouped` return it; the In-House page shows them as the "Storage Location" (Stored tab) and "Discard Method"
  (Discarded tab) columns.

  **Send details on every row.** The row's latest transfer (`transfers[0]`) now also carries
  `externalPartnerName`, `sendDate`, `sendTime`, `sampleForm`, `logisticsType`, `logisticsPerson`, `createdAt`,
  `outsourceCenterId` and the resolved names `destinationBranchName` (INTERNAL) and `outsourceCenterName`
  (OUTSOURCE) - resolved in one batched lookup per page, deactivated branches / centers included; a name is absent /
  null when there is nothing to name. The In-House list shows them in its "Send Details" column.
}
